  data:  # df03
    kind: work_item  # df03
    title: "http/graphql JS linkers hardcode language='javascript' on minted call records"  # df03
    status: todo_hard  # df03
    priority: 2  # df03
    parent:  # df03
    tags:  # df03
    - linker  # df03
    - http_linker  # df03
    - graphql  # df03
    isbefore: []  # df03
    duplicate_of: []  # df03
    not_duplicate_of: []  # df03
    pr_ref:  # df03
    description: "The HTTP and GraphQL client linkers mint HttpClientCall/GraphQLClientCall records with a literal language='javascript' rather than deriving it from the analyzed file/symbol: http.py:689/705/723/745 (_scan_javascript_file) and graphql.py:164 (_scan_javascript_graphql), under packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/. Surfaced in the synthetic-node-stamping family of the 2026-06-10 correctness analysis as a surviving 'language=javascript hardcode class' (strategy Wave-0 B1). Risk: a content-pattern match on non-JS content, or downstream cross-language edges, can carry a mislabeled language. Fix angle: derive language from the symbol/file, or strictly gate the scanners to JS-language files and document the invariant; verify whether the scanners can run on non-JS content before deciding severity."  # df03
    fields: {}  # df03
- op: discuss  # 950d
  at: '2026-09-25T17:49:54Z'  # 950d
  by: agent  # 950d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 950d
  clock: 2  # 950d
  nonce: 950d  # 950d
  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-09-25 (dev e4a47383ab). STILL REPRODUCES, and this answers the row's own open question (\"verify whether the scanners can run on non-JS content before deciding severity\"). Status unchanged.\n\n- The hardcodes are still there, at new line numbers: http.py 705/721/739/761/779/797/817/835/853 (was 689/705/723/745), graphql.py 201 (was 164).\n- Reach: `_find_source_files` (http.py:648-651) globs only py/js/ts/jsx/tsx/go/rb/java/elm. The dispatch at http.py:1400-1411 sends every non-py/go/rb/java/elm file to `_scan_javascript_file`, so that scanner only ever sees .js/.ts/.jsx/.tsx. graphql.py:343-346 is the same, minus the other languages. NON-JS CONTENT CANNOT REACH IT.\n- The real consequence is TypeScript mislabelled as javascript. Fixture a.ts with `return fetch(\"/api/items\")` gives the node `javascript:a.ts:2-2:GET /api/items:call_site` with discovery_language=javascript, on a .ts path. The id's language slot disagrees with the file's language.\n\nSuggested scope: derive the language from the file suffix (ts/tsx -> typescript), as the analyzer does. The \"strictly gate the scanners\" alternative in the description is already true."  # 950d
- op: discuss  # 9441
  at: '2026-10-01T00:54:33Z'  # 9441
  by: agent  # 9441
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9441
  clock: 3  # 9441
  nonce: '9441'  # 9441
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES.\n\nRepro (a.ts `return fetch(\"/api/items\")`, b.tsx `axios.post(\"/api/items\", {})`; survey from /tmp): nodes `javascript:a.ts:2-2:GET /api/items:call_site` and `javascript:b.tsx:3-3:POST /api/items:call_site`, discovery_language=javascript, language=null. Premise holds.\n\nDrift / counts:\n- http.py `_scan_javascript_file` (def :682) has THIRTEEN hardcodes, not 4 (filing) or 9 (09-25 review): lines 705, 721, 739, 761, 779, 797, 817, 835, 853, 873, 891, 909, 929. git blame: all predate filing (2026-01-30 .. 2026-04-17); no commit since 09-25 touched http.py/graphql.py. graphql.py:201 unchanged.\n- Reach unchanged: http.py:642 _find_source_files + dispatch at :1412 (else-branch) and graphql.py:177/:346; only .js/.ts/.jsx/.tsx reach these scanners.\n\nSAME DEFECT, OTHER SPELLING (not in the row): `_detect_language` maps .ts/.tsx -> \"javascript\" in linkers/graphql_resolver.py:191-197, event_sourcing.py:~317, database_query.py:~215, message_queue.py:~284. Not exercised by fixture here (not verified behaviourally).\nPRECEDENT FIX already in tree: websocket.py:362 `_language_for_file` (INV-ronuf clause 3, satisfied) uses core `language_from_path(Path)` to return \"typescript\" for .ts.\n\nProposed: widen scope to \"JS-family linkers label TypeScript files as javascript\" covering http (13 sites), graphql (1) and the four _detect_language helpers; fix via language_from_path as websocket.py does. Title could drop \"hardcode\" (the helpers derive, but wrongly)."  # 9441
- op: update  # cde5
  at: '2026-10-01T01:36:12Z'  # cde5
  by: agent  # cde5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # cde5
  clock: 4  # cde5
  nonce: cde5  # cde5
  set:  # cde5
    title: "JS-family linkers label TypeScript as 'javascript' (http/graphql hardcodes + four _detect_language helpers)"  # cde5
    description: "JS-family linkers label TypeScript as 'javascript' on the records they mint: they either hardcode the literal or derive it from the file suffix with a helper that maps .ts/.tsx to 'javascript'. Under packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/:\n- http.py `_scan_javascript_file` (def ~682): 13 HttpClientCall literals `language=\"javascript\"` at lines 705, 721, 739, 761, 779, 797, 817, 835, 853, 873, 891, 909, 929.\n- graphql.py `_scan_javascript_graphql`: GraphQLClientCall `language=\"javascript\"` at ~201.\n- `_detect_language` helpers that return \"javascript\" for .js/.ts/.jsx/.tsx: graphql_resolver.py ~191, event_sourcing.py ~317, database_query.py ~215, message_queue.py ~284.\nSurfaced in the synthetic-node-stamping family of the 2026-06-10 correctness analysis as a surviving 'language=javascript hardcode class' (strategy Wave-0 B1).\n\nReach: non-JS content cannot reach the http/graphql JS scanners — http.py `_find_source_files` (~642) globs only py/js/ts/jsx/tsx/go/rb/java/elm and the dispatch (~1412) sends only the js/ts/jsx/tsx remainder to `_scan_javascript_file`; graphql.py (~177, ~346) likewise. The real consequence is TypeScript mislabelled as javascript: a.ts `return fetch(\"/api/items\")` gives node `javascript:a.ts:2-2:GET /api/items:call_site` with discovery_language=javascript (b.tsx axios.post likewise). The id's language slot disagrees with the file's language. The four `_detect_language` helpers were not exercised by fixture.\n\nFix: derive the language from the file path the way websocket.py `_language_for_file` (~362, INV-ronuf clause 3) does, via core `language_from_path(Path)` (.ts/.tsx -> typescript), at every site above.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # cde5
- op: discuss  # 300c
  at: '2026-10-01T14:57:28Z'  # 300c
  by: agent  # 300c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 300c
  clock: 5  # 300c
  nonce: 300c  # 300c
  message: "WORK 2026-10-01 (concurrent run; local branch jgstern-agent/fix/komum, commit f0347aa8ea, NOT pushed, status unchanged).\n\nPremise re-verified on dev 4dfb1d645a: http.py 13 literals at 705..929 and graphql.py:201 unchanged; fixture a.ts `fetch(\"/api/items\")` -> `javascript:src/a.ts:2-2:GET /api/items:call_site`, discovery_language=javascript (base survey).\n\nThe four `_detect_language` helpers are NOT one defect: in graphql_resolver/event_sourcing/database_query the value is only a scanner-dispatch key (`elif language == \"javascript\"`) and the minted records already use js_ts_language_from_path (INV-tofun), so those three do not mislabel; left unchanged. message_queue's IS the minted symbol's language -> real mislabel, fixed.\n\nFixed (all via `_text_filters.js_ts_language_from_path`, the analyzer-parity helper, NOT core `language_from_path` as the row proposed: that one returns grammar names, `tsx` for .tsx):\n- http.py 13 sites, graphql.py 1 site, message_queue.py `_detect_language`.\n- js_ts_language_from_path: .mts/.cts -> typescript (it said javascript while claiming to mirror the analyzer; INV-tofun's statement names .mts/.cts; solidity_abi globs .mts).\n- websocket.py `_language_for_file` (the row's cited precedent) minted `tsx:App.tsx:1-1:file:file` for a .tsx file; now typescript.\n\nEvidence: targeted smart-test 5163 passed, 0 failed, changed sources 100% covered. Fixture survey base->after: http call_site on .ts/.tsx javascript->typescript, mq publisher on .ts javascript->typescript, edge sets identical modulo the id slot. Confidence moves: .ts client->typescript route 0.8->0.9; .ts mq publisher->.js subscriber 0.9->0.8 (cross-language penalty now applies to TS<->JS). full-stack-fastapi-template: 23 http call_site nodes relabelled, 0 edges changed (no http edges there before or after). graphql not exercised by survey (linker did not activate on the fixture); covered by link_graphql tests only.\n\n\nResidual items filed: WI-pokij-dizon-bipub-vutiz-dafag-ravid-razog-rikim (annotation_convention grammar-name labels), WI-hizon-matam-gokub-puhab-kabiv-karin-mopot-subat (JS-family linker globs omit .mjs/.cjs/.mts/.cts)."  # 300c
